{
  "id": "COMPOUND:32001 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Koaburaside is implicated in the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Koaburaside acts as a target for multiple compounds, all of which are known to interact with the same set of targets, namely EZH2/SUZ12/EED/RBBP7/RBBP4. These targets are subsequently targeted by Antrocinnamomins A, Quadranoside Viii, and 2''o-Acetylpolygalcin D, all of which are linked to the regulation of the LC-PTP enzyme. This indicates a potential pathway where Koaburaside may influence the activity of LC-PTP through these intermediates. The consistent targeting of LC-PTP across different compounds supports the hypothesis that Koaburaside may modulate LC-PTP function via these intermediates. The mechanism is further supported by the presence of a well-documented mode of action for these compounds, which suggests a plausible biological pathway. The integration of these findings highlights a potential role for Koaburaside in the regulation of LC-PTP, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional impact.",
